Reopen a session's stream when a reconnect gets no answer, and recover the
sandbox status a dropped stream missed.

When the network drops under the session stream without closing it, as a
phone's VPN does when it reconnects, the stream errors and the pump reopens
it at once. That open can sit on a dead route and never get an answer.
Nothing ended it: the stall guard watches only the body, and the wake
fast-path (recycleStreamIfStale) runs only when the tab becomes visible or
the browser comes back online, and neither happens while the app stays in
front. The chat froze until the app was restarted. An open now gives up
after SSE_OPEN_TIMEOUT_MS (10 s, twice the server's slowest answer) and
retries with the usual backoff.

The reconnect's snapshot also didn't restore sandboxStatus. If the sandbox
finished starting while the stream was down, its `ready` event was lost
(the stream has no replay), and the chat kept treating the session as
starting. reconnectStatusPatch now takes it from the snapshot like the
other status fields.

An upstream bug fix: delete it once upstream's startStreamPump times out the
stream open and reconnectStatusPatch sets sandboxStatus.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0031.
